============================================================================
DeepONet smoother -- surface (Laplace-Beltrami) multigrid level
============================================================================
SCOPE: the branch consumes a fixed-length residual, so this model is bound
       to ONE DoF count and ONE DoF ordering -- no cross-mesh claim is made.
       Coefficient-space l^2 is NOT L^2(Gamma): no mass matrix is exported.

Level data: level_data/L4
  A           : 4096 x 4096, nnz 36864 (9.00/row)
  symmetry    : max|A - A^T| = 0.000e+00 -> symmetric
  definiteness: Jacobi-scaled spectrum [3.9413e-03, 2.6747e+00], cond 6.79e+02 -> SPD (sparse factorisation + Lanczos, no densification)
  coordinates : (4096, 3), |x| in [1.0000, 3.0000]
  kappa       : [1.1000, 2.1000]
  ref. edge   : 0 constrained DoFs (uniform mesh)
  prolongation: (4096, 1024)
  MASS MATRIX : not exported -> L^2(Gamma) norms are unavailable; coefficient l^2 is reported instead
  DoFs 4096 -> 64x64 periodic lattice, Nyquist = 32 modes/direction
  trunk features: trig -> dim 4

Hierarchy: 5 levels, DoFs [16, 64, 256, 1024, 4096]
  Galerkin check per level: P^T A_l P versus the separately assembled A_{l-1}
    level 1 -> 0 : max|P^T A P - A_H| = 1.411e+00  (relative 1.907e-01)
    level 2 -> 1 : max|P^T A P - A_H| = 3.716e-01  (relative 4.404e-02)
    level 3 -> 2 : max|P^T A P - A_H| = 7.569e-02  (relative 8.326e-03)
    level 4 -> 3 : max|P^T A P - A_H| = 1.761e-02  (relative 1.899e-03)
  A nonzero difference is expected and is reported rather than hidden: on a
  curved surface the coarse matrix is assembled with the isoparametric
  mapping, and a coarse basis function is not reproduced exactly by the fine
  cells' maps, so the hierarchy is not exactly Galerkin.  The consequence
  for the loss is spelled out below: which A_H it contains is a choice, and
  the two choices do not give the same operator.

Loss target -- the coarse-grid correction the loss simulates:
  restriction      : R = P^T (MGTransferPrebuilt in src/main.cpp), P is 4096 x 1024 (fine x coarse)
  interface/edge   : 0 refinement-edge DoFs -> no edge matrices are applied
  coarse operator  : assembled (1024 x 1024, nnz 9216), spectrum [6.860e-02, 2.208e+01]
  matches the C++ V-cycle operator: YES (assembled A_H)
  densified for the differentiable coarse solve: 8.39 MB; the fine A_h remains sparse throughout

